  "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y+2z}2\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={\u222c}_{D}2[x]_{x=0}^{x=y+2z}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}2(y+2z-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}2y+4z\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}2y+4z\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}2y+4z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}[2yz+2{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=2y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2y(2y)+2(2y)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}4{y}^{2}+8{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}12{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[4{y}^{3}]_{y=1}^{y=3} \\\\  & =4(27-1) \\\\  & =104\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
